1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E06 -= Mikes.Madonna.Story =- Subripped by zerox

2
00:01:02,620 --> 00:01:04,440
这棵植物一定是母的
She's definitely a Wendy.

3
00:01:05,980 --> 00:01:07,500
显然是公的
He is clearly a Sam.

4
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:11,580
爸爸，我自己种的还不清楚吗？ 它是母的
Dad, I think I know my own plant. She's a Wendy.

5
00:01:12,640 --> 00:01:14,720
凯罗，我念过医学
Carol, I went to medical school, okay?

6
00:01:15,175 --> 00:01:17,405
我能找到答案
So, I think I can settle that.

7
00:01:20,740 --> 00:01:21,720
是母的
That's a Wendy.

8
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:25,240
你俩在干什么？
What are you two doing?

9
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:29,960
我在做实验，我一直跟温蒂说话
Well, it's an experiment. I've been talking to Wendy here...

10
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:32,920
另外一棵没名字的不管
and giving what's-his-name the silent treatment.

11
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:35,320
最后看看谁长得快
And well see which one grows faster.

12
00:01:35,800 --> 00:01:39,720
-优胜者会成为今晚的菜 -爸爸!
- And the winner becomes tonights salad. - Dad.

13
00:01:39,720 --> 00:01:42,020
有个女的要找麦克
There's a girl here for Mike.

14
00:01:43,103 --> 00:01:45,435
本，你就让人家站在门外？
Ben, did you just leave her standing outside?

15
00:01:45,520 --> 00:01:48,360
她是个女的，我要怎样？
She's a girl, Mom. What do you want me to do?

16
00:01:48,420 --> 00:01:49,000
让她进来？
Let her in?

17
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:53,540
看来你对女的没什么好感
Sounds like you have some pretty strong feelings about girls.

18
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,520
不，我只是不喜欢她们
No, I just don't like them.

19
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:58,920
本，有朋友来访.
Well, Ben, if a friend comes to the door...

20
00:01:58,920 --> 00:02:02,400
你应该让别人进来
you should let them in.

21
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:06,760
-你好 -你好
- Why, hello. - Hi.

22
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:10,540
-麦克在吗？ -也许在
- Is Mike home? - Possibly.

23
00:02:11,920 --> 00:02:14,600
很可能在，我去看看
Quite possibly. Let me check.

24
00:02:18,271 --> 00:02:19,465
麦姬？
Maggie?

25
00:02:21,100 --> 00:02:23,640
请进
Please, come in.

26
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:25,620
谢谢
Thanks.

27
00:02:29,720 --> 00:02:31,420
随便坐
Would you like to have a seat?

28
00:02:32,200 --> 00:02:34,680
我叫麦姬，麦克的母亲 这是杰森
I'm Maggie, Mike's mother. This is Jason.

29
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:37,260
-你好 -这是本和凯罗
- Hello. - Ben. Carol.

30
00:02:37,700 --> 00:02:39,940
-你呢？ -我叫丽莎
- And you are? - Lisa.

31
00:02:41,027 --> 00:02:43,188
我是麦克的朋友
I'm Mike's, like, friend.

32
00:02:48,500 --> 00:02:51,640
原谅他，他不喜欢女孩子
You have to forgive him, he doesn't like girls.

33
00:02:52,340 --> 00:02:55,640
其实我不把自己当作女孩子
Well, actually, l, like, don't consider myself a girl.

34
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:57,880
我是一个的女人
I consider myself a woman.

35
00:02:58,840 --> 00:03:01,480
说得对
And rightly so, I'm sure.

36
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,540
我去叫麦克
I'll call Mike.

37
00:03:05,340 --> 00:03:06,040
麦克
Mike.

38
00:03:07,900 --> 00:03:09,700
不好意思，他不在家
I'm sorry, he doesn't seem to be here.

39
00:03:17,020 --> 00:03:18,800
或许他也不喜欢女孩子
Guess he doesn't like girls, either.

40
00:03:20,066 --> 00:03:21,863
走着瞧
Well see about that.

41
00:03:27,500 --> 00:03:29,309
丽莎，吃点什么吗？
So, Lisa. Dip?

42
00:03:29,309 --> 00:03:30,571
-不了 -不？
- No. - No.

43
00:03:33,740 --> 00:03:34,580
丽莎.
Hey, Lisa...

44
00:03:36,716 --> 00:03:38,707
真让人喜出望外
what a pleasant surprise.

45
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:43,120
我刚好经过，我要跟男朋友分手
I was just in the neighborhood, breaking up with my old boyfriend.

46
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,280
-是吗？ -是的
- Oh, yeah? - Yeah.

47
00:03:45,458 --> 00:03:47,323
他太幼稚了
He was just too immature.

48
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:53,400
-他岁数比你小？ -不，他27岁
- Was he younger than you? - No, he was 27.

49
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,220
真巧.
What an amazing coincidence...

50
00:03:56,469 --> 00:03:59,597
我刚打电话跟女朋友分手
cause I was just up on the phone, breaking up with my old girlfriend.

51
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,620
她43岁
She was 43.

52
00:04:03,420 --> 00:04:05,140
是啊，以狗的年龄来算
Yeah, in dog years maybe.

53
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:12,060
你们也很久没探望史蒂夫伯伯了
You guys haven't seen Uncle Steve in a while.

54
00:04:12,140 --> 00:04:13,440
就去看望一下他吧
Why don't you go take a walk by his place?

55
00:04:14,560 --> 00:04:16,500
麦克，史蒂夫伯伯住在新疆
Mike, your uncle Steve's in Connecticut.

56
00:04:18,220 --> 00:04:18,660
那怎样了？
So?

57
00:04:20,020 --> 00:04:21,160
而且他去世了
And he's dead.

58
00:04:25,400 --> 00:04:26,760
你们去吃点什么吗？
Should you guys go have a snack?

59
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:30,340
好吧，咱们走
Right, okay. All right, come on, guys.

60
00:04:31,020 --> 00:04:33,160
-丽莎，幸会 -幸会
- Lisa, very nice to meet you. - You, too.

61
00:04:38,780 --> 00:04:39,660
麦姬，再见
See you, Maggie.

62
00:04:42,440 --> 00:04:44,460
直呼你的名字没关系吧？
You don't mind if I call you Maggie, do you?

63
00:04:46,586 --> 00:04:47,610
没关系
No.

64
00:04:52,320 --> 00:04:55,500
爸爸，那女孩穿得真是的
God, Dad, do you believe the top that girl was wearing?

65
00:04:56,800 --> 00:04:57,720
我没注意到
I didn't notice.

66
00:05:00,440 --> 00:05:03,160
拜托，差不多等于没穿上衣
Come on, Dad, she might as well have had no shirt on at all.

67
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:05,720
权衡轻重.
Well, all things considered...

68
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:07,820
幸好她还没到那种地步
I'm glad she didn't choose to go that route.

69
00:05:08,020 --> 00:05:08,740
我同意
Me, too.

70
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:13,120
凯罗，带本出去玩吧
Carol, why don't you take Ben and go outside.

71
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:16,660
-为什么？ -因为我要跟爸爸谈谈
- Why? - Because I need to talk to your father.

72
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:19,300
关于麦克滥交朋友？
About Mikes friend with the major-league yabos?

73
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:22,000
你们俩出去
Out! Both of you.

74
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:24,200
出去干什么呢？
What are we supposed to do outside?

75
00:05:24,200 --> 00:05:25,880
随便，跟草地说话吧
I don't care. Talk to the lawn.

76
00:05:26,040 --> 00:05:27,820
或者剪剪草
No. it needs mowing as it is.

77
00:05:33,380 --> 00:05:35,780
那女孩穿得真是的!
Did you see the top that girl was wearing?

78
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:39,380
杰森，她是个婊子
Jason, she's a tramp.

79
00:05:40,420 --> 00:05:41,460
不是吧
Come on, Maggie.

80
00:05:42,180 --> 00:05:45,460
我承认她确实穿得.
No. I mean, I admit she doesn't dress with a lot of....

81
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,000
她是没穿
Clothing.

82
00:05:47,620 --> 00:05:48,120
没有品味
Taste.

83
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:50,680
但我们还不了解她
But we don't know anything about the girl.

84
00:05:51,080 --> 00:05:53,880
她跟27岁的人交往
Jason, she was going out with a 27-year-old.

85
00:05:54,260 --> 00:05:55,540
这样就成婊子了？
And that makes her a tramp?

86
00:05:56,240 --> 00:05:58,440
也许他们是志同道合
Well, maybe they shared the same interests.

87
00:05:58,940 --> 00:06:00,340
那正是婊子的行为
That makes her a tramp.

88
00:06:00,593 --> 00:06:01,958
麦姬.
Oh, Maggie.

89
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:04,140
杰森，她连笑起来.
Jason, she doesn't even giggle...

90
00:06:04,140 --> 00:06:05,980
也不像一个15岁的女孩子
the way a 15-year-old is supposed to giggle.

91
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:08,700
好，我去通知国防部
Well, I'll call the National Guard.

92
00:06:09,820 --> 00:06:11,520
你也懂我意思
You know what I mean.

93
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:15,600
当一个15岁的女孩上门找我儿子时.
When a 15-year-old girl comes to my door, asking for my son...

94
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:17,600
她应该感到局促不安
she should feel awkward and uncomfortable.

95
00:06:18,140 --> 00:06:20,700
但这次是我感到局促不安
With this girl, I feel awkward and uncomfortable.

96
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,381
瞧，她笑了
See, she giggles.

97
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,800
我刚说错了
My mistake.

98
00:06:32,692 --> 00:06:36,685
你们能不能出去一下？
So, do you think you guys could leave?

99
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:41,280
-为什么？ -好让我们和果汁
- Why? - So we can have some juice.

100
00:06:42,100 --> 00:06:44,080
我们在屋里就不能喝？
You mean, you can't have juice with us in the room?

101
00:06:45,220 --> 00:06:48,500
你们买下9个房间的屋子.
Fine, fine. But I don't know why you guys bought a house with nine rooms...

102
00:06:48,500 --> 00:06:49,560
怎么都不使用呢？
if you're not gonna use them.

103
00:06:51,740 --> 00:06:52,360
说得够婉转
Subtle, Mike.

104
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:58,800
就这样，我对埃德说分手 他，他哭了
So anyway, when I told Ed I was breaking up with him, he, like, cried.

105
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:02,915
-可怜虫 -确实是
- it was so pathetic. - Yeah, that is pathetic.

106
00:07:04,056 --> 00:07:05,956
我从来不哭
l, like, never cry.

107
00:07:06,360 --> 00:07:06,880
真的？
Really?

108
00:07:08,600 --> 00:07:11,100
除了那次被车碾到脚
Well, once when a car rode over my foot, I winced.

109
00:07:12,960 --> 00:07:14,660
麦克，你真帅
You're, like, so cute, Mike.

110
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,720
怎么说呢？
Hey, what can I say?

111
00:07:17,680 --> 00:07:20,800
帅就是一个字
Yeah, I'm cute. I'm damn cute.

112
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:27,760
埃德也太多心了
Plus, Ed was like super possessive.

113
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:31,240
我只是跟菲尔去露营，他就生气了
I mean, he, like, got upset because I went camping with Phil Crawly...

114
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:34,540
-基本上只是朋友关系 -基本上？
- who's, like, just a friend, basically. - Basically?

115
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:36,020
-妈妈 -对不起
- Mom. - I'm sorry.

116
00:07:38,300 --> 00:07:38,720
丽莎.
Lisa...

117
00:07:40,020 --> 00:07:43,760
你跟27岁的人交往，父母怎么看？
so how did your parents feel about you going out with a 27-year-old?

118
00:07:44,380 --> 00:07:46,420
-我妈妈很不满意 -是吗？
- Like, my mother, she was bummed. - Really?

119
00:07:46,660 --> 00:07:48,440
也许她想跟他交往
Like, I think she wanted to go out with him.

120
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:56,340
那你父母离婚了？
I take it your parents are no longer together then?

121
00:07:56,760 --> 00:08:00,560
-为什么？ -没什么，算了
- What makes you say that? - Nothing. Never mind.

122
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:07,540
好，麦克，今晚有节目吗？
So, like anyway, Mike, you wanna do something tonight?

123
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:13,680
刚才我刚分手了
Well, I did just end a very special relationship.

124
00:08:13,720 --> 00:08:16,560
我也跟她胡混够了
But I think I've moped around about that long enough.

125
00:08:21,080 --> 00:08:23,320
别忘了我和你爸 今晚要和库斯曼家出去.
Mike, don't forget that your father and I are going out...

126
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:25,900
你要负责照顾本和凯罗
with the Koosmans tonight, and you have to baby-sit Ben and Carol.

127
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:28,180
找个保姆行吗？
Can't we get a sitter?

128
00:08:28,740 --> 00:08:30,540
这么急去哪里找？
On this short notice, not one without an axe.

129
00:08:32,411 --> 00:08:35,244
本和凯罗逃命的功夫其实很好
So? Ben and Carol are quick on their feet.

130
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:39,260
-麦克 -好吧
- Mike? - Okay, okay.

131
00:08:39,760 --> 00:08:42,680
或者今晚我过来这里吧
Hey, Mike, maybe I could, like, come over here tonight.

132
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:44,500
那样.
Yeah! That'd be--

133
00:08:44,500 --> 00:08:47,640
丽莎这个周末就太枯燥了
Probably a very boring way for Lisa to spend a Saturday night.

134
00:08:47,727 --> 00:08:51,754
不枯燥，我喜欢当保姆
No, it wouldn't be boring, Maggie. I just love baby-sitting.

135
00:08:54,540 --> 00:08:56,000
这个女人真好
What a woman, huh, Mom?

136
00:08:57,880 --> 00:08:59,100
确实
You betcha.

137
00:09:05,820 --> 00:09:08,560
你是世界上最坏的植物
You are the ugliest plant alive.

138
00:09:10,349 --> 00:09:13,250
凯罗悄悄对我说她讨厌你
Carol told me privately that she hates you.

139
00:09:18,958 --> 00:09:22,485
-本，你在干什么？ -没什么
- Ben, what are you doing? - Nothing, Mom.

140
00:09:25,940 --> 00:09:27,980
-好了吗？ -好了
- Okay, all set? - Yeah.

141
00:09:28,420 --> 00:09:30,620
-跟他谈话了？ -对
- So? Did you talk to him? - Yeah.

142
00:09:31,003 --> 00:09:32,600
他怎么说了？
Well, what did you say?

143
00:09:32,600 --> 00:09:34,780
跟我们说的差不多
Well, pretty much what you and I discussed.

144
00:09:35,040 --> 00:09:36,900
具体怎么说？
Like what, specifically?

145
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:40,060
就是那种父子谈话
Well, you know, it was one of those father-son talks.

146
00:09:40,740 --> 00:09:44,100
原谅我，我没体验过那种谈话
Forgive me, Jason. I have never had one of those father-son talks.

147
00:09:44,900 --> 00:09:49,080
-你怎么说？ -我问他.
- What did you say? - Well, that's where I say:

148
00:09:50,780 --> 00:09:52,600
还好吗？“ 他回答：”很好
"How you doing, Son? " He says, "Pretty good, Dad."

149
00:09:52,680 --> 00:09:54,680
我问：“你头上喷了定型喷雾..”
I say, "Is that mousse in your hair, or is it wet--"

150
00:09:55,027 --> 00:09:57,188
杰森，说重点
Jason, get to the good part.

151
00:09:57,720 --> 00:09:59,780
我告诉他大体上.
Honey, I just told him that in general...

152
00:09:59,780 --> 00:10:02,720
关系应该慢慢地培养
I think that it's better to start slowly with a relationship...

153
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:05,660
要了解那个人，还要.
to get to know somebody, to get a--

154
00:10:05,660 --> 00:10:08,680
-验艾滋病 -对，那个也要
- A medical report. - That, too, I guess.

155
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:11,360
那么.
So....

156
00:10:12,520 --> 00:10:13,900
他们今晚打算怎样？
Well, what do you think they'll do tonight?

157
00:10:14,540 --> 00:10:17,080
很可能看电视吧
Well, they'll probably watch TV.

158
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:23,900
如果他们不看电视呢？
Jason, what if they don't watch TV?

159
00:10:25,320 --> 00:10:28,920
才15岁，15岁的男女会看电视？
I mean, he's only 15. He's too young to not watch TV.

160
00:10:29,620 --> 00:10:34,240
若是15岁的少男少女不想看电视.
Well, if two teenage kids want to get together and not watch TV...

161
00:10:34,533 --> 00:10:36,831
他们总会想到办法做别的事情
they're gonna find a way to do it.

162
00:10:36,920 --> 00:10:38,460
我累了，今晚不出去了
I'm tired. Let's stay home.

163
00:10:38,838 --> 00:10:41,329
-麦姬 -我要看电视<爱之船>
- Maggie. - I wanna watch The Love Boat.

164
00:10:43,180 --> 00:10:45,480
鲍勃和艾伦3分钟后就来接我们了
Bob and Ellen are picking us up in three minutes.

165
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:47,600
我们真的不该留下？
Are you sure we shouldn't stay home?

166
00:10:48,840 --> 00:10:53,380
你得明白，不管我们走到哪里.
You know, what you have to remember is that no matter where we are...

167
00:10:53,380 --> 00:10:56,620
麦克脑里都会有把声音.
there's always that little voice inside Mike's head...

168
00:10:56,620 --> 00:11:00,920
“麦克，我是你妈妈..”
saying, "Mike, this is your mother speaking."

169
00:11:03,040 --> 00:11:05,700
麦克会诧异“妈，你找我干什么？”
And that's when Mike says, "Ma, what are you doing here? "

170
00:11:05,860 --> 00:11:11,280
那把声音回答“我要提醒你..”
And the little voice says, "l just want to remind you that I love you...

171
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:13,340
“我一直都会很疼爱你”
"and I'll always love you...

172
00:11:14,460 --> 00:11:19,020
“即使你和那女孩胡来”
"even if you break my heart by touching that girl somewhere."

173
00:11:22,180 --> 00:11:25,480
你是指我让他产生愧疚感.
Okay, okay. So you're saying I've already saddled him with enough guilt...

174
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:26,920
一辈子摆脱不了？
to cripple him for life?

175
00:11:28,454 --> 00:11:31,685
不，我是指他知道我们的价值观
No. I'm saying that he knows our values...

176
00:11:31,720 --> 00:11:33,580
他知道我们疼爱他
and he knows that we care about him.

177
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:36,020
面对人生的重大抉择时.
And I know that he will consider that...

178
00:11:36,228 --> 00:11:38,924
他会慎重考虑
anytime he makes one of life's big decisions.

179
